# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses f4c9d13865f3, 2026-10-19
# Berkeley's well-known equivocation is between heat as a felt sensation and heat as a quality in the object. Here, though, every statement says "perceived by sense", so no single claim shifts sense.
# The weak point is the step in A1 from the bearer of heat to the feeler of pain. That step links two claims; it is not one claim used in two senses.
heat_is_pain	one
perceives	one
capable_pain	one
subject_heat	one
